# Swan Compiler 2 — SIL Demand Analysis
#
# Analyze which SIL values, declarations, and computations are demanded by
# observable program behavior.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Compute value-use and def-use relationships.
# - Track demanded results through branches, joins, and function boundaries.
# - Distinguish pure computations from side-effecting operations.
# - Preserve observable effects, traps, required initialization, and ownership
#   operations even when their produced values are unused.
# - Provide liveness and demand facts to SIL optimization.
#
# Analysis must be conservative: uncertainty keeps an operation live.
# It must never remove a side effect merely because its result is unused.
#
# Implementation status: contract; analysis is not implemented yet.
